data: {"id":9,"jsonrpc":"2.0","result":{"content":[{"text":"Returned:\nAgent: 112a6ce7-7642-43f3-adc8-7538ea4032c3\n\nDepends on who's asking for it — if it's just a nice-to-have nobody's requested, I'd hold off; if users or the team have actually asked, it's usually a small win since most CSS frameworks support it cheaply via a `prefers-color-scheme` media query plus a manual override stored in localStorage. The main tradeoff is upkeep: every new UI component has to be tested in both themes going forward, which adds ongoing QA surface for a purely cosmetic feature. Want me to check if there's an existing story or user request for this before we scope it?\n","type":"text"}],"isError":false}}

